From: Selman Trabzon <selman.trbzon@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 01:24:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] feat: player settings as data for foreseerr's own ui

The page asks the app for Moonfin's player settings over a promise bridge,
foreseerrPlayer.request(). Nothing lists settings by hand: the screens under
Playback come from Moonfin's settings search index, each is built off-screen,
and every standard preference tile on it is read back with its key, labels,
options and current value. Changes go through the tile's own preference and
callbacks, after the sign-in settings sync has landed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
